# Derived by hand from Conformance AB (a tick that aborts leaves the state as it was before the tick, and the World goes on) and the counter's rule: the wrong answer to the button is no click, so its tick aborts, and the next click counts from 1 to 2; a job pending across an aborted tick takes its four cycles (D6) in the ticks after it.
test the_world_goes_on_after_an_abort

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="Increment")
    1: Ui.Label(text="Count: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="Count: 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: "oops"
  aborted
  | Runtime.Answer: expected a Click, got "oops"

tick 3
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="Count: 2")

test a_job_goes_on_after_an_abort

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="poke")
    2: Ui.Label(text="working")

tick 1
  in:
    0: "oops"
  aborted
  | Runtime.Answer: expected a Click, got "oops"

compute until idle: 4 ticks, 2 to 5

tick 5
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="7")
